  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mekong for the Future</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(China):  .The Mekong for the Future activity addresses the PRC government&apos;s policies and initiatives that negatively affect the sustainable management of natural resources in the Mekong region. The activity aims to increase transparency and access to data and information, and promote participation of civil society organizations in natural resources management. By increasing civil society participation in these processes, environmental governance in the region can become more inclusive, accountable, and transparent. FY 2021 funds will be used to engage with stakeholders, such as non-government organizations (NGOs), civil society organizations (CSOs), and media to strengthen their organizational capacity for policy analysis and advocacy, and promote CSO engagement in the decision-making processes. This greater transparency and inclusiveness will broaden the range of stakeholders holding their governments accountable and advocating for better policies to manage natural resources in a more sustainable manner at the national and regional levels... .</narrative>
  </description>
